Usage: agent-deck watcher create <type> --name <name> [options]

Types: webhook, ntfy, github, slack

Creates a watcher under a name it does not already hold. If the name is
already registered, or a watcher.toml for it already exists, this command
fails: agent-deck never overwrites a watcher config. Edit that file to
change an existing watcher's settings.

Options:
  -name string
    	Watcher name (required)
  -no-secret
    	webhook only: accept unsigned requests from local processes (not recommended)
  -port int
    	Port for webhook adapter
  -random-topic
    	Generate a random, hard-to-guess topic for ntfy or slack adapter
  -secret string
    	DEPRECATED/insecure: use $GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET / $WEBHOOK_SECRET or --secret-file
  -secret-file string
    	Path to a chmod-600 file holding the github or webhook secret (webhook: generated when not given)
  -server string
    	ntfy server URL for ntfy or slack adapter (default https://ntfy.sh)
  -token-file string
    	Path to a chmod-600 file holding an ntfy access token (or set $NTFY_TOKEN)
  -topic string
    	Topic for ntfy or slack adapter
